Backend Architecture
Version: 2026-07-23
Status: Authoritative Backend Guide

Overview
This document describes the backend architecture of WordList Writer. It merges the original backend specification with updated Phase 2 architecture rules, July 19 fixes, and the hybrid master list model. It explains how Express is structured, how API routes connect to controllers, how Supabase is integrated, and how save and load pipelines operate. It also documents rules that keep frontend and backend interaction stable. WordList Writer is a teacher-facing authoring tool. Students never interact with the application. All UI components, including frequency lists, cognates, master lists, warnings, and project tools, are designed exclusively for teacher use.

High-Level Structure
The backend is a lightweight Express server. It provides:
* static file hosting
* API routes for saving and loading data
* Supabase integration for persistence
* middleware for JSON parsing and routing
The backend does not perform text analysis. All analysis occurs in the frontend.

Server Entry Point
The backend entry point is:
src/server.js
Responsibilities:
* initialize Express
* register middleware
* register API routes
* serve static files
* start HTTP server

Middleware Order
Middleware order is critical:
* JSON body parser
* API routes
* static file hosting
Static hosting must come last. If placed earlier, it will shadow API routes.

API Route Structure
API routes live in:
src/routes
Each route file:
* defines endpoints
* imports controllers
* exports router
Example route types:
* /api/project/save
* /api/project/load
* /api/master/save
* /api/master/load

Controllers
Controllers live in:
src/controllers
Responsibilities:
* validate request data
* call Supabase client
* transform results
* return JSON responses
Controllers must not contain business logic.

Supabase Client
Supabase client lives in:
src/lib/supabase.js
Responsibilities:
* create Supabase client instance
* expose client for controllers
Environment variables required:
* SUPABASE_URL
* SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY

Database Tables
Supabase stores:
* projects
* project_wordlists
* master_wordlists
Full schema is documented in:
docs/Supabase_Schema.md

SaveEverything Workflow
Steps:
Step 1: save project metadata
Step 2: capture returned project id
Step 3: save project wordlist
Step 4: save master list
Step 5: return success response
This order must never change.

Load Workflow
Steps:
Step 1: load project metadata
Step 2: load project wordlist
Step 3: load master list
Step 4: return combined JSON
Frontend rebuilds UI state.

Error Handling
Backend error handling rules:
* always return JSON errors
* never crash server
* log Supabase errors
* validate request bodies
* validate project id

Static File Hosting
Static files live in:
public/
Server uses:
express.static("public")
Static hosting must be registered after API routes.

Adding New API Routes
When adding new routes:
* create route file in src/routes
* create controller in src/controllers
* update API_Specification.md
* update Docs_Index.md

Safe Coding Practices
* never mix analysis logic into backend
* always validate inputs
* always check Supabase errors
* always return JSON
* keep controllers small
* keep route files simple

Hybrid Master List Model
The curriculum system uses four coordinated vocabulary layers:
* global master list defines universal curriculum backbone
* language master lists provide frequency ranking and multilingual support
* context master lists provide optional curriculum modes
* project master lists track vocabulary progression inside a single story
The system compares vocabulary across layers to enforce curriculum rules.

Project List Architecture
* project list is auto-generated from story text
* always reflects normalized lemmas in story order
* never saved to Supabase
* regenerated on every tokenization
* used for story-order insertion logic

Master List Architecture
* master list stores English lemmas only in Phase 2
* stored values are normalized strings
* UI displays "Capitalized English" but underlying value is the lemma
* master list is saved to Supabase
* master list is loaded only when user loads a project
* master list is not auto-populated from story text

Master List Insertion Logic
Steps:
Step 1: normalize the English lemma
Step 2: find last master list lemma appearing in the story
Step 3: insert new lemma immediately after that position
Step 4: prevent duplicates by comparing normalized lemmas
Step 5: render updated master list

Tokenizer Pipeline
* tokenizeUnified normalizes tokens into stable lemmas
* tokenizeUnified returns objects only for real word tokens
* punctuation and whitespace remain raw strings
* tokenizeUnified must not trigger highlight or autosave
* tokenizeUnified must not log normalized tokens

Cognate System (Phase 2)
* simple cognate window remains active
* cognates detected directly from normalized tokens
* no object storage for cognates
* no tier-based highlighting in Spanish mode
* no structural changes to master list
* click-to-insert adds English lemma only
* Spanish lemma ignored for insertion
* no multilingual canonical switching
* no curriculum impact beyond English lemma insertion

Cognate Detection Rules
* detectCognates must set english = normalized lemma
* detectCognates must not produce empty english fields
* cognate window displays Spanish -> English pairs
* updateCognates must call requestHighlightUpdate
* updateCognates must not call handleStableInput

Phase 2 Constraints
* English-only master list
* Spanish cognates used only for detection
* no multilingual insertion
* no multilingual canonical switching
* no curriculum-level cognate objects
* no structural changes to master list format

Highlight Pipeline Rules
Centralized Highlight Pipeline:
* all highlight operations must enter through requestHighlightUpdate
* handleStableInput must never be called directly from event listeners
* requestHighlightUpdate uses debounce
* no other function may trigger highlight
* no highlight or tokenizer runs during IME composition
* highlight runs only after IME commits text

IME Input Rules:
* compositionstart sets isComposing true
* compositionend sets isComposing false and triggers requestHighlightUpdate
* no tokenizer or highlight runs during composition
* IME safety prevents prefix logs and double tokenization

Startup Highlight Sequence:
* startup triggers highlight once
* project list and order check run after highlight
* recommended delay is 75ms
* prevents double tokenization and flicker

Startup Frequency Loop Removal:
* triggerFrequencyLoop must not run on startup
* frequency stats computed inside handleStableInput
* no frequency scanning before first highlight

Debug Logging Rules:
* remove normalized token logs
* remove lemmaMap prefix logs
* remove sample frequency logs
* no tokenizer logs in production
* only "Load complete" allowed on startup

Autosave Rules
* autosave must be debounced
* autosave must not run inside input handlers
* autosave pauses during project resets
* autosave resumes after reset completes

Frequency List Rules
* frequencySet must be loaded before highlight pipeline
* frequencySet must contain normalized lemmas only
* frequency stats computed inside handleStableInput

July 19 Fixes
Project ID Rules:
* project-id-input must update when a new project is created
* project-id-input must update when a project is loaded
* loadEverything writes currentProjectId into project-id-input
* saveEverything writes currentProjectId into project-id-input
* New Project writes currentProjectId into project-id-input
* without this, loadEverything receives null and master list loads empty

Master List Save Rules:
* masterList contains plain strings
* apiSaveMasterList must send raw strings
* mapping item.lemma or item.word is invalid
* Supabase insert must receive rows like { project_id, lemma }
* undefined values cause silent rejection
* correct mapping: rows = [...masterListArray]

Master List Load Rules:
* loadEverything calls apiLoadMasterList(projectId)
* load route returns { success: true, data: [...] }
* masterList assigned directly from returned data
* master list rendered after assignment

Frequency Known-Word Rules:
* known words come from NGSL-1K
* master list is not a known-word list
* using master list for known-word detection marks all words unknown
* correct known-word set: new Set(frequencyData.map(item => normalizeLemma(item.lemma)))
* restores green checks
* enables cognate highlighting

Workflows Summary
SaveEverything Workflow:
Step 1: save project metadata
Step 2: capture project id
Step 3: save project wordlist
Step 4: save master list
Step 5: return success response

Load Workflow:
Step 1: load project metadata
Step 2: load project wordlist
Step 3: load master list
Step 4: return combined JSON

Summary
This backend architecture document explains how Express is structured, how API routes and controllers work, how Supabase is integrated, and how save and load pipelines operate. It merges updated Phase 2 architecture rules, July 19 fixes, and the hybrid master list model to ensure stable interaction between frontend and backend. The system supports English-only master lists, lightweight cognate detection, stable tokenizer behavior, and predictable highlight operations for teacher-facing workflows.
